{
  "vector_set": "telemetry",
  "version": "v1",
  "source": "spec v1 §9.10; master plan §3.5 'Telemetry'; sdk-v0 plan §2.1 'Telemetry batcher'; D14, D16, D39; reference Part 6 §11 (Go parseUsage, rows go-*: parity/fixtures/proxy/unit.json#parse_usage); crates/maverick-core/src/telemetry.rs, crates/maverick-core/src/chain.rs, crates/maverick-domain/src/telemetry.rs. Hand-checked.",
  "rules": {
    "item": [
      "One item per dispatched attempt. A skipped entry (no request sent) has no item.",
      "recommendation_id is the recommend response's id; model_used is the entry's catalog model (in OpenRouter mode too, not the slug).",
      "status is the HTTP status, or 0 when the transport failed; then error_class is timeout (no response headers within the attempt timeout) or connect_error (any other transport failure). error_class is absent when a status arrived.",
      "latency_ms is the whole milliseconds until the response headers arrived or the transport failed.",
      "tokens_in and tokens_out are present only for a 2xx whose body was buffered (not streamed), read by the usage rules for the surface.",
      "endpoint_used is direct or openrouter. A component may omit it when it is direct: the engine reads absent as direct.",
      "check_pass is present only when a check ran (D16); it is never defaulted.",
      "settings_applied is always present: true when at least one entry setting was written to the request (D14).",
      "No prompt, completion, request body, or credential is ever part of an item."
    ],
    "usage": [
      "The body must be a JSON object. usage absent or null means no counts. usage of any other non-object type means no counts.",
      "chat_completions reads usage.prompt_tokens and usage.completion_tokens; messages reads usage.input_tokens and usage.output_tokens.",
      "Each count must be a JSON integer; null is absent and 0 is kept. If either field of the surface is present with another type (a string, or a number with a fraction), both counts are absent."
    ],
    "outcome": [
      "The engine decodes each item alone and drops (and counts) a malformed one: recommendation_id and model_used must be non-empty strings, status an integer >= 0; latency_ms, tokens_in, tokens_out integers >= 0 when present; error_class one of timeout, connect_error, provider_error, other; endpoint_used one of direct, vertex, bedrock, azure, openrouter (absent is direct); check_pass and settings_applied booleans when present.",
      "First matching rule: error_class timeout is latency_exceeded; error_class connect_error or provider_error, status 0, 429, or 5xx is provider_error; a 2xx is parse_failure (check_pass false), success (check_pass true), or completed_unchecked (no check_pass); anything else is other."
    ]
  },
  "how_to_run": "usage_cases: read the body with each surface's rule; null means absent. attempt_cases: derive the item from the attempt and compare as JSON objects (an item without endpoint_used equals one with endpoint_used direct). outcome_cases: these are the engine's rules, for reference; a core does not run them.",
